==English==
[[File:Geranium wilfordii (sepal).JPG|thumb|{{center top}}The '''perianth''' of this flower includes the pale [[petal]]s and the green [[sepal]]s. The flower's organs hidden behind the petals in this photograph, namely the [[stamen]]s and [[pistil]], are not part of the '''perianth'''.{{center bottom}}]]
[[File:Blepharostoma trichophyllum (d, 144542-474731) 9814.JPG|thumb|{{center top}}A mature spore of the [[liverwort]] {{taxlink|Blepharostoma trichophyllum|species}} in its '''perianth'''{{center bottom}}]]

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|fr|périanthe}}, from {{der|en|NL.|perianthium}}. {{surf|en|peri-|-anth}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} The [[sterile]] parts of a [[flower]]; collectively, the [[sepal]]s and [[petal]]s (or [[tepal]]s).
# {{lb|en|botany|bryology}} The sterile, tubelike [[tissue]] that surrounds the female reproductive structure in a leafy [[liverwort]].
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=5|text=Archegonia are surrounded early in their development by the juvenile '''perianth''', through the slender beak of which the elongated neck of the fertilized archegonium protrudes.}}

